<title>SINGAPORE: Shangri La Hotel 1st-half net up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Shangri La Hotel 1st-half net up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless specified)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     9.45 vs  7.88</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cts)	     5.00 vs  5.00</p>
<p>    Special dividend (cts)	     5.00 vs   nil</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (EPS) (cts)   6.30 vs  5.25</p>
<p>    Turnover				71.11 vs 64.78</p>
<p>    Investment income		    4.12 vs  5.96</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    25.90 vs 23.97</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   3.59 vs  2.95</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	  7.20 vs  6.44</p>
<p>    Loss from associates		 1.47 vs  3.00</p>
<p>    Tax					4.00 vs  3.73</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (loss) 0.18 vs  0.03</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	     (loss) 0.62 vs 37.57 (gain)</p>
<p>Note - Full name is Shangri La Hotel Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
